\section*{Impact Statement}
This paper studies how to compute shorter, still valid, confidence intervals from machine-learning predictions. Its main societal consequence is better calibrated uncertainty in scientific and administrative estimates; it also shows settings where the intervals do not cover, which should reduce overconfident use. We see no further specific concerns.

